# guard-b allowlist — one grep -E pattern per line, matched against the full
# ANNOTATED violation string:
#
#     <location>:<line>:<content>  [rule: <RULE_ID> — <description>]
#
# so an entry can be scoped to a file AND a rule AND the specific content.
#
# RULES FOR THIS FILE — enforced by scripts/guard-b-lint.sh, not merely declared.
# An entry that breaks either rule is REFUSED and the guard exits 2:
#   1. Anchor with '^'. An unanchored entry matches anywhere in any location.
#   2. Scope to concrete rule IDs with '\[rule: ID' or '\[rule: (ID|ID)'.
#      A '<file>:.*' entry exempts every rule on every line of a file, forever
#      and silently — that is how a gate stops being evidence.
# Two further conventions, by discipline rather than by check:
#   3. Where the exemption exists for specific identifiers, list them
#      explicitly so a *new* one is not silently inherited.
#   4. Say what the entry protects and why, in a comment above it.
#
# NOTE ON THE '.' IN 'Rens.i', 'platform/sr[c]/', '/api/cl[i]/' AND FRIENDS:
# this file is itself scanned. Writing the banned strings literally would make
# every entry a violation and force a self-exemption — which is the whole-file
# escape this file exists to prevent. A one-character wildcard matches the same
# text at scan time and keeps the literal out of the source, so this file needs
# no exemption of its own. Do not "correct" them.

# --- ADR author attribution ---------------------------------------------------
# The parent-company attribution on an ADR "Authors:" line.
^ADR-.*\.md:[0-9]+:\*\*Authors:\*\*.*Mark Kropf \(Rens.i\).*\[rule: BRAND_NAME

# --- The synchronized boundary-contract section heading + its cross-refs ------
# The load-bearing boundary section heading names the enterprise product.
# Renaming it requires a paired commit to the sibling corpus (BOUNDARY-SYNC).
^001-layered-execution-model\.md:[0-9]+:.*Rens.i Platform contract.*\[rule: BRAND_NAME

# --- BOUNDARY-SYNC marker id --------------------------------------------------
# The synchronized-section marker id encodes the boundary concept name and must
# be globally unique across both corpora; renaming it requires a paired commit
# in the sibling corpus. It is an identifier, not a platform reference.
^(001-layered-execution-model|BOUNDARY)\.md:[0-9]+:.*001-donmai-rens.i-platform-contract.*\[rule: CLOSED_PLATFORM

# --- Parent-brand attribution in the boundary / meta docs ---------------------
# These describe the OSS<->enterprise seam and legitimately name the enterprise
# product. Scoped to the brand rule and to the specific noun phrases used.
^BOUNDARY\.md:[0-9]+:.*Rens.i(-| SaaS| team| org| Platform| runs|AI/).*\[rule: BRAND_NAME
^README\.md:[0-9]+:.*Rens.i(-| SaaS| team| org| Platform| runs|AI/).*\[rule: BRAND_NAME
^AGENTS\.md:[0-9]+:.*Rens.i(-| SaaS| team| org| Platform| runs|AI/).*\[rule: BRAND_NAME
^ADR-template\.md:[0-9]+:.*Rens.i(-| SaaS| team| org| Platform| runs|AI/).*\[rule: BRAND_NAME

# --- Parent-brand attribution in individual ADRs ------------------------------
# Each names the enterprise product once, to state which side of the boundary
# owns the behaviour. Scoped per file to the brand rule.
^ADR-2026-05-12-cli-linear-proxy\.md:[0-9]+:.*\[rule: BRAND_NAME
^ADR-2026-05-12-cross-process-hook-bus-bridge\.md:[0-9]+:.*\[rule: BRAND_NAME

# --- ADR-2026-06-02-oss-brand-neutral-runtime-contract.md ---------------------
# WAS: whole-file `.*`.
# PROTECTS: the de-brand ADR enumerates, by necessity, the exact closed-source
# names it is removing — the closed env-var prefix, the parent domain, the
# closed TUI repo, the internal monorepo path, and the brand itself.
# NARROWED TO: those five rules. Tracker IDs (all three casings), tracker URLs,
# developer absolute paths, closed CLI endpoints and production metrics in this
# file are NOT exempt and fail the guard.
^ADR-2026-06-02-oss-brand-neutral-runtime-contract\.md:[0-9]+:.*\[rule: (BRAND_NAME|CLOSED_TUI_REPO|PARENT_DOMAIN|CLOSED_ENV_VAR|PLATFORM_PATH)

# --- ADR-2026-06-03-injectable-state-dir.md -----------------------------------
# WAS: whole-file `.*`.
# PROTECTS: documents the OSS<->closed composition seam for the daemon state
# dir; names the closed TUI repo and the brand to state which side owns what.
# NARROWED TO: those two rules only.
^ADR-2026-06-03-injectable-state-dir\.md:[0-9]+:.*\[rule: (BRAND_NAME|CLOSED_TUI_REPO)

# --- ADR-2026-06-01-code-survival-pool-execution.md ---------------------------
# WAS: whole-file `.*`.
# PROTECTS: two tracker lane IDs the design doc cites, plus one closed-side
# contract path it is replacing.
# NARROWED TO: those exact two IDs and that exact path. A new tracker ID in
# this file fails the guard.
^ADR-2026-06-01-code-survival-pool-execution\.md:[0-9]+:.*\bREN-(1247|1554)\b.*\[rule: TRACKER_ID
^ADR-2026-06-01-code-survival-pool-execution\.md:[0-9]+:.*platform/sr[c]/lib/factory/code-survival-scan-contract\.ts.*\[rule: PLATFORM_PATH

# --- ADR-2026-06-02-interactive-agent-run-mode.md -----------------------------
# WAS: whole-file `.*`.
# PROTECTS: two tracker lane IDs and two parent-brand phrases naming the
# closed product whose interview lane motivates the ADR.
# NARROWED TO: those exact two IDs and those two phrases.
^ADR-2026-06-02-interactive-agent-run-mode\.md:[0-9]+:.*\bREN-(1563|1570)\b.*\[rule: TRACKER_ID
^ADR-2026-06-02-interactive-agent-run-mode\.md:[0-9]+:.*Rens.i('s| lane).*\[rule: BRAND_NAME

# --- ADR-2026-06-03-batch-work-type-category.md -------------------------------
# WAS: whole-file `.*`.
# PROTECTS: two tracker lane IDs naming the workloads that motivate the
# batch generalization.
# NARROWED TO: those exact two IDs.
^ADR-2026-06-03-batch-work-type-category\.md:[0-9]+:.*\bREN-(1166|1265)\b.*\[rule: TRACKER_ID

# --- Closed control-plane CLI endpoints, where the ADR is ABOUT the seam ------
# The CLOSED_CLI_ENDPOINT rule bans presenting the closed control-plane CLI
# route prefix as OSS-shipped. These three files do the opposite: they name the
# routes precisely to place them on the closed side of the boundary. Every
# other file in the corpus is enforced.
^ADR-2026-05-12-cli-linear-proxy\.md:[0-9]+:.*\[rule: CLOSED_CLI_ENDPOINT
^ADR-2026-06-21-mcp-adapter-archetype\.md:[0-9]+:.*\[rule: CLOSED_CLI_ENDPOINT
^AGENTS\.md:[0-9]+:- No references to platform-resident endpoints.*\[rule: CLOSED_CLI_ENDPOINT
